      "message": "Yes, it will cause CtsStatsdAtomHostTestCases fail.\nhttps://partnerissuetracker.corp.google.com/issues/346909845\n\n\nThis rootcause for the case fail is when calling UiAutomation.adoptShellPermissionIdentity, it will  call AppOpsService.setCheckOpsDelegate and set mAccessCheckDelegate  not null.\n\nPermissions.replacePermissionsWith(Permissions.kt:79) -\u003e\nUiAutomation.adoptShellPermissionIdentity(UiAutomation.java:615) -\u003e\nAppOpsService.setCheckOpsDelegate\n\n\n\nBut when close-\u003erestorePermissions, it didn\u0027t reset mAccessCheckDelegate to null, this will lead to case fail. So, we think restorePermissions should call dropShellPermissionIdentity to reset mAccessCheckDelegate.\n\nPermissions.withPermissions(Permissions.kt:41) -\u003e \nclose -\u003e \nrestorePermissions(savedPermissions)",
